WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:06.000
Rats are crawling all over the "House of the
Dragon," but are they just a metaphor, or something more?

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.288
And where have we seen that mysterious red
flower before?

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:14.320
For several weeks in a row, various rodents
have scurried in and out of frame on "House

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.400
of the Dragon."

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.679
In Episode 6, Viserys spots a mouse on a mantle
as he's alone in his bedchamber, as viewers

00:00:20.679 --> 00:00:24.640
hear Larys tell Queen Alicent about the weakness
of children.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:29.039
But the most overt inclusion of a rat is the
one that drinks the recently deceased Ser

00:00:29.039 --> 00:00:34.800
Joffrey Lonmouth's blood as Rhaenyra and Laenor
exchange their vows in Episode 5.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.390
Many readers of "Fire &amp; Blood" feel like the
rats are an indicator of an upcoming plotline

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:45.285
that, if the show follows the book, would
be a huge spoiler, so we'll say no more about that here.

00:00:45.285 --> 00:00:49.900
But King's Landing's prominent vermin problem
might have another explanation.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.239
Though there's no textual evidence for this
theory in George R.R.

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:58.489
Martin's writing, Reddit moderator and YouTuber
Joe Magician has laid out the possibility

00:00:58.489 --> 00:01:02.870
that a character on "House of the Dragon"
could be a skinchanger like Bran Stark.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:07.480
If so, the rats could be being used to spy
and gather information.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:13.070
Ten years on, it seems like every move mortal
enemies Princess Rhaenyra and Queen Alicent

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:14.780
make is a power play.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:18.790
Episode 6 opens with Rhaenyra's delivery of
her third child.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:23.600
Just about the moment the midwife places the
baby in the princess' arms, a messenger arrives

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.170
to take the newborn to the queen's chambers.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:29.579
Rhaenyra will not have her son separated from
her so quickly.

00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:34.051
Before she's even passed the placenta, she
dresses to make the long walk through the Red Keep.

00:01:34.051 --> 00:01:39.020
Her husband, Laenor Velaryon, accompanies
her and holds her upright as she has to stop

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:41.790
each time she has an afterbirth contraction.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:47.159
During one of these moments on the stairs,
Lord Caswell and his lady wife approach Rhaenyra

00:01:47.159 --> 00:01:48.242
and Laenor enthusiastically.

00:01:48.242 --> 00:01:51.149
"If I may be of any service?"

00:01:51.149 --> 00:01:53.873
"The day may yet come, my lord."

00:01:53.873 --> 00:01:58.369
This seems like a subtle bit of foreshadowing
on the show's part, as prominent families

00:01:58.369 --> 00:01:59.950
begin to take sides.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:04.770
House Caswell appears to be staunchly loyal
to Rhaenyra as tension and uncertainty about

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:10.604
the succession mounts, and that loyalty will
likely soon be tested in dramatic fashion.

00:02:10.604 --> 00:02:15.390
After Rhaenyra wills herself to the queen's
private quarters, she presents the newborn

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:21.120
prince to Alicent, who's basically become
her evil stepmother, and her father King Viserys,

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.140
who's shockingly still alive, though just
barely.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.370
Viserys is genuinely happy to meet the child
and remarks that he thinks the boy has his

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.690
father's nose.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:33.860
When the queen asks what they'll call him,
Rhaenyra begins to say they haven't decided,

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:39.188
but then Laenor bursts out the name "Joffrey"
which probably made "Game of Thrones" fans perk up.

00:02:39.188 --> 00:02:43.960
But the name is a reference to another murdered
Joffrey from nearly two centuries prior, and

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.390
Alicent can't hide her feelings about it.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:48.660
"That's an unusual name for a Velaryon."

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:53.980
With this polite-enough sounding comment,
Alicent is actually making two accusations.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:58.840
Though we only met him briefly, Joffrey was
the first name of Laenor's lover — Ser Joffrey

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:03.770
Lonmouth, the Knight of Kisses — who was
brutally murdered by Ser Criston Cole at the

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:06.110
welcome feast in Episode 5.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:11.070
Laenor and Joffrey's relationship was an open
secret, at least at Driftmark and probably

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:12.530
even at King's Landing.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:16.440
Still, for the queen to underscore the fact
that the future king consort wants to name

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:20.590
his purported son after his murdered boyfriend
is remarkably bold.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:25.400
Alicent is also implying that she knows this
child, like the previous two, isn't really

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.580
Laenor's, since she's well aware of his sexual
preferences.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.784
"Do keep trying, Ser Laenor.

00:03:31.784 --> 00:03:34.675
Sooner or later, you may get one who looks
like you."

00:03:34.675 --> 00:03:39.070
King Viserys' small council has changed considerably
over the years.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:43.290
Corlys Velaryon has been replaced by Tyland
Lannister as Master of Ships.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:47.980
When Otto Hightower was dismissed as Hand
of the King, Lyonel Strong was chosen to fulfill

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:49.760
that most important role.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:53.730
Only Lyman Beesbury remains in his original
position of Master of Coin.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:58.000
But two of the most noticeable changes to
the king's council are the addition of his

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.650
daughter, Princess Rhaenyra, and his wife,
Queen Alicent.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:06.870
Rhaenyra was promoted from cupbearer to council
member after being named heir and Princess

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:07.870
of Dragonstone.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:13.180
A decade later, a much more politically active
Alicent also has a seat at the table.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:17.910
Production designers conceived of small spheres
to signify a character's presence at the small

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:23.369
council table, each in colors that represent
the great houses to which the council members belong.

00:04:23.369 --> 00:04:27.760
Queen Alicent sits behind a green ball that's
reminiscent of Hightower's colors and her

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:33.090
infamous gown, while Rhaenyra rolls her fingers
across a black one for House Targaryen.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:38.270
These totems demonstrate that both have accumulated
immense power in the last decade, regardless

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:40.350
of their opposition to each other.

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:44.420
Earlier in the season, it was frowned upon
for the princess to speak at all when she's

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:47.630
with the lords behind the closed doors of
the small council room.

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:53.500
Now, she and Alicent are practically running
the show, though they seem to disagree about everything.

00:04:53.673 --> 00:04:58.690
We met Lyonel Strong's sons, Harwin and Larys,
during the hunt in Episode 3.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:03.160
Larys has since ingratiated himself to Queen
Alicent by becoming her unofficial Master

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:08.910
of Whisperers while Harwin has entangled himself
in some deadly serious palace drama by fathering

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.650
Rhaenyra's three children.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:14.600
Savvy viewers will have noticed that Harwin
was quite taken with Rhaenyra after she killed

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:18.270
the boar, and when she donned boys' clothing
on the Streets of Silk.

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:22.710
He's also the one who carries her to safety
after the melee at the welcome feast.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:27.090
Larys doesn't seem to have a very high opinion
of his father, the Hand, or his brother.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:31.420
When Queen Alicent complains that King Viserys
wouldn't accept Lyonel's resignation after

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:37.310
Harwin attacks Ser Criston in the training
yard, Larys graduates from whispers to actions.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:41.810
Lyonel takes Harwin to the family seat of
Harrenhal, which is said to be cursed, to

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:44.870
avoid persistent rumors of the princes' parentage.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:49.370
Meanwhile, Larys frees some of King's Landing's
most dangerous prisoners, so long as they're

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:52.980
okay with him cutting off their tongues so
they can't spill the beans.

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:57.680
He sends his assassins to Harrenhal to murder
his father and brother via arson, which he

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:02.310
tells a horrified Alicent that she'll thank
him for later, as he holds the foreign flower

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:04.299
to which he previously compared her.

00:06:04.299 --> 00:06:09.360
"An outsider, among the natives."

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:13.000
"Lord Larys."

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:17.780
In "Fire &amp; Blood," Larys isn't just Master
of Whisperers; he's Lord Confessor.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:22.630
That title is a euphemism for torturer-in-chief,
so it's no surprise to book readers that he's

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:25.400
so eager to break out the tools of his trade.

